@bank all
// 0.99.91 piece C (TB7 for lead 51): the Wednesday drill as Chief Calder's talk at the Works bay muster line
// (TB9991_DRILL_ON, section 24c's drill9991). Stand-ins, the same as the game's fallbacks; a writer replaces them (same
// keys). Calder: plain, brisk, fair. A card line is 90 characters at most. Per kind (fire, pressure, power): the card's
// title, six lines in order, the crew line (Zeke for fire, Halloran for pressure; none for power) and her close.

== drill9991.toast.fire
- Drill at 15:00: the fire drill. Muster at the Works bay.
== drill9991.toast.pressure
- Drill at 15:00: the pressure drill. Muster at the Works bay.
== drill9991.toast.power
- Drill at 15:00: the power drill. Muster at the Works bay.

// the fire drill
== drill9991.goal.fire
- Fire drill, 15:00: Chief Calder at the Works bay
== drill9991.fire.title
- Fire drill
== drill9991.fire.line.1
- Right. Fire drill. In close, everyone.
== drill9991.fire.line.2
- Fire hurts us fastest out here. No window to open. Nowhere to go but the next deck.
== drill9991.fire.line.3
- Smoke is worse than flames. It fills a room in a minute and takes the air with it.
== drill9991.fire.line.4
- Extinguishers: red, by every hatch. Pin out, aim at the base of it, short sweeps.
== drill9991.fire.line.5
- Bigger than you? Don't fight it. Shut the hatch on it, call the bridge, get people out.
== drill9991.fire.line.6
- And nobody goes back in for their things. Things we can replace.
== drill9991.fire.crew
- Three real ones in twenty years. Every one of them started as somebody's toaster.
== drill9991.fire.close
- That's the drill. On the line with us till the all-clear.

// the pressure drill
== drill9991.goal.pressure
- Pressure drill, 15:00: Chief Calder at the Works bay
== drill9991.pressure.title
- Pressure drill
== drill9991.pressure.line.1
- Pressure drill. Listen up.
== drill9991.pressure.line.2
- A breach is quiet at first. A whistle. Your ears pop. Paper starts sliding toward a wall.
== drill9991.pressure.line.3
- It isn't the cold. It's the air leaving. You get seconds of good sense, then less.
== drill9991.pressure.line.4
- Bulkhead doors close a leak off. The wheel on the door: four turns, dogged tight.
== drill9991.pressure.line.5
- Don't wait to see who's on the other side. Close it. The bridge counts heads after.
== drill9991.pressure.line.6
- Ears pop and you're on your own? Nearest door, shut it behind you, then call.
== drill9991.pressure.crew
- Dog it, then shout. Never the other way round. Shouting doesn't hold air.
== drill9991.pressure.close
- That's the drill. On the line with us till the all-clear.

// the power drill
== drill9991.goal.power
- Power drill, 15:00: Chief Calder at the Works bay
== drill9991.power.title
- Power drill
== drill9991.power.line.1
- Power drill. This one's ours more than anyone's.
== drill9991.power.line.2
- Main bus drops: the lights go, the air scrubbers slow, the lifts stop where they are.
== drill9991.power.line.3
- The danger is people hurrying in the dark. Stairs and panic hurt more than the dark.
== drill9991.power.line.4
- The breaker cabinet puts the junior wing on reserve. Air and strip lights. Not much else.
== drill9991.power.line.5
- Never open a live panel to have a look. Reserve bites as hard as main.
== drill9991.power.line.6
- Stand still. Let your eyes adjust. Follow the floor strips to your muster point.
== drill9991.power.close
- That's the drill. On the line with us till the all-clear.

// the tip at the line, a tap before three, the notice after her talk, a missed drill, the Friday tea (the turnout)
== drill9991.tip
- Tap Chief Calder to join the drill
== drill9991.early
- Three o'clock, on the muster line. Not yet.
== drill9991.notice
- You stand on the muster line with the Works team till the all-clear at 15:15.
== drill9991.missed
- We ran the drill without you. Next Wednesday, three o'clock, Works bay.
== drill9991.tea
- Good turnout at Wednesday's drill. Thank you, all of you.
